        "category": "offensive",
        "description": {
            "value": "<p><em>The Art of the Libra Tridents.</em></p><p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are wielding both @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra Trident (Right)] and @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra Trident (Left)]</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within your reach uses a move action, or leaves a square within your reach</p><hr /><p>Strike it with a trident. On a hit its movement <strong>immediately ends</strong>; on a critical hit it is also pushed 10 feet and knocked <strong>prone</strong>.</p><p><strong>Greater (8th level)</strong> Your reach with the Tridents becomes <strong>15 feet</strong>, and the Art also triggers on a <strong>manipulate</strong> action; on a critical hit, that action is <strong>disrupted</strong>.</p><p><strong>Perfect (14th level)</strong> You gain <strong>one additional reaction each round</strong>, usable only for Setting the Tide &mdash; which is what the second use per round below is.</p><hr /><p>Granted by @UUID[Compendium.isaacs-hb-pf2e.saint-class-features.Item.Libra — the Weapons]. Target the creature that moved and use this: the Strike is rolled for you, and a critical hit pushes it and puts it down.</p><p><em>Automation note: from 8th level the Tridents trade pf2e's flat <strong>reach</strong> trait for <strong>reach 15 ft.</strong>, a trait this module registers, because pf2e's own reach is +5 feet and cannot say fifteen.</em></p>"
        },
